    <statement><p>Find an equation of the line passing through the points <m>(6,-5)</m> with the slope <m>m = {{\frac{4}{7}}}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="32" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><ul label="disc">
<li>
<p>Do not use decimal approximations in your answer.</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</statement>
    <hint><p><em>Hint:</em> Use the point-slope form of a line. <m>y = m (x-x_A) + y_A</m></p>
</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y = \frac{4}{7}\mathopen{}\left(x-6\right)-5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><alert>Use the point-slope form of a line:</alert></p>
<p><m>y = m (x - x_A) + y_A</m></p>
<p><m>y = {{\frac{4}{7}}\mathopen{}\left(x-6\right)-5}</m></p>
</solution>
